        ":question/id": "157038e6-e68d-5ec0-b464-27301542d833",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-18188",
        ":question/problem": "![](images/98/98b3193783f0ac19bcb78035b133ad8dbf956528dfb7474606cc586d3bfecc34.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $90{\\text{ in}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
        ":question/requires-calculator": true,
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =168\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘} \\\\  & =139.278… \\\\  & ≈139{\\text{ in}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of  $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =139-90 \\\\  & =49{\\text{ in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      "parameters": {
        "a": 16,
        "b": 21,
        "angle": 56,
        "quadrilateral": 90,
        "unit": "in",
        "orientation": 0
      }
    },
